  ('eaa580a0-19f3-5de0-aafa-312fe36a33a5', 'language', 'What language was most commonly spoken at Fez around 789 AD?', 'Arabic and Amazigh (Berber) were both widely spoken; Arabic was the language of the Idrisid court and administration', ARRAY['Greek (Koine Greek), the language of the city''s Greek founders and administration, alongside Egyptian spoken by the native population', 'Unknown / undeciphered - recorded only in the still-untranslated Indus script', 'An early form of Tongan, a Polynesian language']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('eaa580a0-19f3-5de0-aafa-312fe36a33a5', 'inventions', 'What craft industry, still operating today at Fez''s centuries-old Chouara Tannery using traditional stone-vat methods, has made the city famous?', 'Traditional leather tanning', ARRAY['Birch bark documents (berestyanye gramoty)', 'Glazed ceramic roof tiles (and traditional wooden bracket/dougong construction)', 'Medicine, mathematics, astronomy, and botany']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('eaa580a0-19f3-5de0-aafa-312fe36a33a5', 'world_firsts', 'What Guinness World Record does Fez''s University of al-Qarawiyyin hold?', 'Oldest existing, continually operating degree-granting university in the world', ARRAY['The site of Europe''s first advanced (Bronze Age) palace civilization, the Minoans.', 'It became one of the first states in the world, and the first major African kingdom, to officially adopt Christianity', 'He calculated the circumference of the Earth with remarkable accuracy']::text[], false, null, null),
