  ('08b2fc9e-8407-5d4f-ae4a-c6e0b6683ced', 'inventions', 'What did the Kilwa Sultanate become one of the earliest sub-Saharan African states to do, starting in the medieval period?', 'Mint its own silver and copper coins', ARRAY['The double-shell (double-dome) construction technique', 'Birch bark documents (berestyanye gramoty)', 'The sakdina system, a hierarchical land-and-labor-based social ranking system']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('08b2fc9e-8407-5d4f-ae4a-c6e0b6683ced', 'world_firsts', 'Coins minted at Kilwa Kisiwani centuries ago have been found as far away as which distant continent, revealing the reach of its Indian Ocean trade network?', 'Australia (a Kilwa coin was found on the Wessel Islands)', ARRAY['It is often cited as the second-largest city square in the world, after Tiananmen Square in Beijing.', 'They form one of the largest collections of geoglyphs in the world, spanning roughly 450+ square kilometers.', 'The Meroitic script']::text[], false, null, null),
