  ('4ccfeeef-5791-5fe0-8634-ec29b2d7ac19', 'flag_meaning', 'What does the maple leaf on Canada''s national flag represent?', 'Canada and national unity - it was deliberately chosen as a race-, language-, and region-neutral emblem.', ARRAY['The monarchy (part of the national motto ''Nation, Religion, King'').', 'Islam, agriculture, and the prosperity of the land', 'The Swahili people, native to Tanzania and its majority population']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('4ccfeeef-5791-5fe0-8634-ec29b2d7ac19', 'language', 'What language was most commonly spoken at Quebec City around 1608 AD?', 'French, spoken by Champlain''s colonists (Algonquian and Iroquoian languages were spoken by the Indigenous peoples of the surrounding region)', ARRAY['Ge''ez, the classical Ethiosemitic language of the Aksumite Kingdom', 'Swahili (Kiswahili), a Bantu language enriched with Arabic loanwords through Indian Ocean trade', 'Old East Slavic (the local Old Novgorod dialect), alongside Finnic languages spoken by neighboring tribes']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('4ccfeeef-5791-5fe0-8634-ec29b2d7ac19', 'inventions', 'What seasonal accommodation, North America''s only ice hotel, is rebuilt near Quebec City every winter?', 'The Hotel de Glace (Ice Hotel)', ARRAY['The double-shell (double-dome) construction technique', 'Reservoirs and check dams (such as the Far View Reservoir)', 'One of the world''s earliest known flushing toilets, alongside a piped water and drainage system']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('4ccfeeef-5791-5fe0-8634-ec29b2d7ac19', 'world_firsts', 'What is the Quebec Winter Carnival billed as, in terms of scale?', 'The largest winter carnival in the world.', ARRAY['The site of Europe''s first advanced (Bronze Age) palace civilization, the Minoans.', 'They provide one of the most complete dynastic histories of any Classic Maya city, thanks to unusually extensive carved texts.', 'It was the second-largest city in Europe (after Constantinople), with a population estimated around 400,000.']::text[], false, null, null),
