  ('b64e0795-f8af-5723-b0fa-97d7e20c4137', 'flag_meaning', 'What does the eagle devouring a serpent atop a cactus, at the center of Mexico''s flag, represent?', 'The Aztec founding legend of Tenochtitlan, in which this sign revealed the divinely chosen site for the Aztec capital.', ARRAY['The monarchy (part of the national motto ''Nation, Religion, King'').', 'Impartiality and sovereignty (added in 1920 to distinguish the flag from Poland''s, and originally also representing Moravia and Slovakia).', 'The 13 original British colonies that became the first U.S. states']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('b64e0795-f8af-5723-b0fa-97d7e20c4137', 'language', 'What language was most commonly spoken at Palenque around 615 AD?', 'A Classic Maya (Western/Ch''olan) language, ancestral to modern Ch''ol', ARRAY['Arabic (Andalusi Arabic), alongside Mozarabic Romance spoken by the local Christian population', 'Unknown - the Nazca had no writing system, so their spoken language is not preserved in the historical record', 'Czech, alongside German (widely used among the city''s substantial German-speaking population and Latin-using clergy/scholars)']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('b64e0795-f8af-5723-b0fa-97d7e20c4137', 'inventions', 'What advanced water-engineering feat did Palenque''s builders achieve, centuries ahead of comparable technology elsewhere in the Americas?', 'A pressurized underground aqueduct system - the earliest known in the Americas', ARRAY['A university (Charles University, the first university in Central Europe)', 'The mercury amalgamation ("patio") process', 'Reservoirs and check dams (such as the Far View Reservoir)']::text[], false, null, null),
  ('b64e0795-f8af-5723-b0fa-97d7e20c4137', 'world_firsts', 'What makes Palenque''s hieroglyphic inscriptions especially significant among Maya sites?', 'They provide one of the most complete dynastic histories of any Classic Maya city, thanks to unusually extensive carved texts.', ARRAY['The largest winter carnival in the world.', 'It is the oldest university in Central Europe.', 'The world''s first surf lifesaving club (the Bondi Surf Bathers'' Life Saving Club, founded 1907).']::text[], false, null, null),
